==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱh₂d-}}
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|récidivisme}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|recidīvus||returning, recurring}}. Compare {{m|en|recidivous}}, {{af|en|-ism}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Committing new [[offense]]s after a [[crime]] committed in the past.
#: ''The increase in criminal activity was attributed to [[recidivism]].''
# {{lb|en|psychology|psychiatry}} [[chronic|Chronic]] [[repetition]] of [[criminal]] or other [[antisocial]] behavior.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Returning to a negative [[behavior]] after having stopped it for a period of time.
#: ''alcohol(ic) '''recidivism'''''

